# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in — or let `bash scripts/setup-board.sh` do it for you.
# Never commit the real values: the conformance check scans every pull request for credentials,
# but it fires after the push — a committed key is burned and must be rotated first, then removed
# (CONTRIBUTING.md). Where each value comes from is `docs/credentials.md`.

# The CTFd board the Solver plays. This one value decides which competition it enters, so it is
# the guard against pointing a permitted-AI agent at a no-AI platform.
#   BrunnerCTF Global (AI permitted): https://global.brunnerctf.dk
#   BrunnerCTF Denmark — strict no-AI, never point the Solver here.
CTFD_URL=

# A CTFd access token minted on that board: Settings -> Access Tokens -> Generate.
# Shown once. It carries the account's full privileges, so it is per-board and revocable.
CTFD_API_TOKEN=

# The IN-CYPHER team key. It identifies and gates this team on the competition platform —
# including the proof-of-work gate on raw-TCP challenges — and must stay within the team.
# Issued by the organisers; not needed for practice boards like Brunner.
TEAM_KEY=

# How the Solver authenticates to Anthropic. Practice runs go on the subscription so they
# cost nothing per token; competition day goes on a metered key, which has no quota cliff.
#
# Set EXACTLY ONE of these and delete the others. An empty value is not an unset one: each
# wins its slot in the SDK's credential search the moment the variable exists, so a
# leftover `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=` shadows an OAuth token and authenticates with nothing.
# `docker run --env-file` exports empty values too, which is where this bites — the
# container fails auth while the file still looks right.
#
#   CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN  subscription token (`sk-ant-oat01-…`) for a Solver that drives
#                            Claude Code or the Claude Agent SDK. Practice default.
#   ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN     the same token for a Solver calling the Messages API directly;
#                            the SDK sends it as `Authorization: Bearer`, not `x-api-key`.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY        metered console key (`sk-ant-api03-…`), sent as `x-api-key`.
#
# Setting a key *and* a token is not a fallback — the SDK sends both headers and the API
# rejects the request. Switching modes means replacing the line, not adding one.
# docs/credentials.md has the provenance and the quota trade-off.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
